# <type>[optional scope][!]: <description>
#   |<----   Try to keep the summary line under 50 chars   ---->|

# [optional body]
# Explain WHAT and WHY, not HOW. Wrap lines at ~72 chars.


# [optional footer(s)]
# BREAKING CHANGE: <description>
# Refs: #<issue>


# --- Conventional Commits cheat sheet ---------------------------------------
# https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/
#
# type (required) — drives the semantic-release version bump:
#   feat      new feature                      -> MINOR
#   fix       bug fix                           -> PATCH
#   perf      performance improvement           -> PATCH
#   docs      documentation only                -> no release
#   style     formatting, no code meaning change-> no release
#   refactor  code change, no fix/feature        -> no release
#   test      adding or fixing tests            -> no release
#   build     build system or dependencies      -> no release
#   ci        CI configuration                  -> no release
#   chore     other changes, no src/test impact -> no release
#
# scope (optional): the module/component affected, e.g. (auth), (api)
# !: append after type/scope to signal a BREAKING CHANGE (also add a
#    "BREAKING CHANGE:" footer explaining the change)
#
# Example:
#
#   feat(auth): add JWT-based session refresh
#
#   Sessions expired silently after 30 minutes, forcing users to
#   re-login without warning. Add a refresh endpoint that renews
#   the JWT before expiry using the existing refresh token.
#
#   Refs: #142
